## Releasing

`.github/workflows/release.yml` publishes to PyPI when you push a tag that matches the
project version, using [trusted publishing](https://docs.pypi.org/trusted-publishers/);
no token is stored. Once, before the first release: on PyPI, add a trusted publisher
for this repository with workflow `release.yml` and environment `pypi`, and create the
`pypi` environment in the repository settings.

```bash
uv version 0.2.0      # bump the version, commit, and merge
git tag v0.2.0 && git push origin v0.2.0
```

